# Qwen3.8's ubatch card route on real text: the same binary, BLOOMERY_QWEN38_EXPERTS=card against the all-host plan,
# both arms fed the first P ids of the profile's prose corpus (prose:<P>), under BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 so the host
# arms' `stat prompt38 lb` rows carry the prose routing's per-expert column counts (the lcg prompt's routing is
# heavily skewed — rig-log 09-29 #q38mhist-read — and pseudo-random ids say nothing about text).
# Derived on the lcg rows (rig-log 09-29 #q38route-pp): a layer-batch is rest + union, rest 3.5 / 36 ms at
# P = 512 / 4096, all-host union 29.1 / 252 ms, the card route under the union's shadow. With the card's share s of
# the routed slots on the 43 card layers, their union is about 1.03 (1 - s) of the all-host one (the lcg ratio of
# union to slots) and the five host-only layers stay whole: at s = 0.45..0.65, +53..+105 % at P = 512 and
# +51..+100 % at P = 4096 [derived]. The lcg prompt's s was 0.554 / 0.522.
# Wall [derived]: 4 arms x 2 rounds of fresh loads (40..90 s) plus prompts and warm primes: 15..22 min.
kind: ab
question: does the ubatch card route lift Qwen3.8's prefill on prose as the card's share of the prose routing says?
term: pp tok/s @ P = U = 512 and 4096 on corpus-prose.ids (prose:<P>), A6000, BLOOMERY_QWEN38_EXPERTS=card against
  the host plan, same binary, paired by round, BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 on both arms
unit: %
predict: +50..+105
rounds: 2
condition: BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 BLOOMERY_WARM_ROWS=1 BLOOMERY_THREADS=32
  BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/q38prose-pp.card' just depth-gpu-qwen4exp prose:512
  prose:512@BLOOMERY_QWEN38_EXPERTS=host prose:4096 prose:4096@BLOOMERY_QWEN38_EXPERTS=host (the bare arms are the
  card plan, the lever's default; the ratio lines are card/host), the full output to a file
  first; the card arms' plan line experts=card, load line card_layers=43; no counted row [cold] or [other-busy]
decide-in: the card share on prose is what the host slots say: land nothing new; read the host arms' spread
  (m_hot, cols_hot, R) as the prose histogram and price a router-frequency list and q38down (reports/q38hostonly §2) on it
decide-below: the prose routing puts less than 0.45 of its mass on the id prefix: a router-frequency list is the next lever
  (its worth is the top-n_l mass the host rows give); compute it before any run
decide-above: more than 0.65 on the prefix: the prefix is near the list's value on prose; q38down (the five
  host-only layers) and the prefill group come before a router-frequency list
